# Vauxhall Mokka X compact SUV, 2016-2021.
#
# The Mokka X: the facelifted J13 body with the new grille, the redesigned
# lamps and a new dashboard. UK showrooms from October 2016; replaced by the
# Mokka B in April 2021.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Mokka
#
# Dimensions 4.280 x 1.775 x 1.646 m, wheelbase 2.555 m. The Mokka X is the
# same J13 body and no separate dimension table was read, so these are the
# Mokka A figures and the height is grade (c).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation of a Mokka X was found; the
# Mokka A side is used for the body and the X-specific nose and lamps come
# from the front views, with the limitation recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the New Mokka X 2017 Models Edition 1 of August 2016:
# Royal Blue solid, Summit White and Lava Red brilliant, and Quantum Grey,
# Amaretto, Sovereign Silver, Boracay Blue and Mineral Black metallic.
# Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 72/438, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 72. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro October 2016; retires staggered 2018-2021 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-x.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-mokka-x.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-mokka-x/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the shared Mokka A flank and glazing are used, because
# no side elevation of a Mokka X exists; the X-specific nose, grille, lamps and
# bumper are taken from the X pack. Lamp graphics and brightwork are
# simplified, and the rear glass and skid plate keep the Mokka A
# simplifications.


